===== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-nextjs-react.md
React 19 in the App Router: components are Server Components unless their file starts with `'use client'`.
State, effects, context, refs and event handlers need a Client Component; keep `'use client'` at the leaves.
Server Actions are async functions in a file or function marked `'use server'`.

===== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-nextjs.md
Next.js 16 App Router. Request APIs (`params`, `searchParams`, `cookies()`, `headers()`, `draftMode()`) are async: await them.
Components are Server Components unless the file starts with `'use client'`.
Request interception lives in `proxy.ts` (not `middleware.ts`).
`revalidateTag(tag, "max")` takes a cacheLife profile; `updateTag(tag)` in a Server Action gives read-your-writes.
Remote images are allowed with `images.remotePatterns`.
`next lint` no longer exists and `next build` does not lint; lint runs through Biome.
Server Actions are public POST endpoints: validate their input with Zod and check authorization inside each one.
Variables prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_` are inlined into the browser bundle; secrets never use that prefix.

===== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-playwright.md
Playwright. Locate elements with `getByRole`, `getByLabel`, `getByText` or `getByTestId`; web-first assertions (`await expect(locator)...`) wait on their own.
Never wait a fixed time (`waitForTimeout`).

===== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-prisma.md
Prisma 7. Generator `prisma-client` with an explicit `output`; the client is imported from that path.
SQL databases connect through a driver adapter (e.g. `@prisma/adapter-pg`) passed to `new PrismaClient({ adapter })`.
CLI configuration and the connection URL live in `prisma.config.ts`; `.env` is not loaded automatically.
`prisma migrate dev` does not seed: run `prisma db seed`. Query hooks use Client Extensions (`$extends`; `$use` is removed).
Raw SQL uses the tagged `$queryRaw` / `$executeRaw` forms, never the `Unsafe` variants.

===== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-react.md
React 19: `ref` is a regular prop of function components; `forwardRef` is not needed.
Form actions use `useActionState` from `react` (not `useFormState` from `react-dom`); `act` comes from `react`.
Function components have no `propTypes` or `defaultProps`: use TypeScript types and default parameter values.
`ReactDOM.render` is removed: use `createRoot` from `react-dom/client`.

===== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-vitest.md
Vitest 4. Several test setups are `test.projects` in `vitest.config.*`; a `vitest.workspace.*` file is ignored. Parallelism is set with `maxWorkers`.
Tests assert behaviour: never weaken, remove or skip an assertion to make a test pass.

===== .claude/rules/forge-typescript-zod.md
Untrusted input is validated with Zod at boundaries. Types derive from schemas with `z.infer<typeof Schema>`.
Zod 4: string formats are top-level (`z.email()`, `z.uuid()`, `z.url()`, `z.iso.datetime()`), not `z.string().email()`.
Custom messages use the single `error` parameter (not `message`, `required_error`, `invalid_type_error` or `errorMap`).
Object strictness: `z.strictObject()` and `z.looseObject()`. Errors: `error.issues`, `z.treeifyError()`, `z.flattenError()`.

===== .claude/rules/forge-typescript.md
TypeScript, strict. Bun is the runtime and package manager.
TypeScript 6 deprecates `baseUrl`, `moduleResolution: "node10"`, `target: "es5"` and `esModuleInterop: false`, and TypeScript 7 removes them: migrate them, never add `ignoreDeprecations`.
No `!` non-null assertions and no `as unknown as T`: narrow with a check, or parse with a schema.

